"epic choice row" is a notebook page
	<header level="1">
		&lt;epic-choice-row&gt;
		<header>One row of a choice page: a use site, the box holding Claude's recommendation, and a comment box.</>
	</>

	<text class="lede" paragraph>One row of a choice page: the use site, what it's for, how it reads today, and a box pre-filled with Claude's call, which you type over or leave. Under the box, a comment box for your choice or notes on that row alone; the row's note, Claude's short why, is a column of its own, last.</>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>
		For anyone writing a page you answer on (a details or choice page), or changing this element.

		<label size="mini" color="green">built</> in <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-choice-rows" link="/epic/src/components/epic-choice-rows/"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-choice-rows/" code>epic-choice-rows/</></> (epic <text code>epic-workflow</> P12; the comment box and the Explanation column, epic <text code>epic-engine</> P58).

		Its vocabulary (every table below comes from it): <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-choice-rows-epicchoicerow-en-ts" link="/epic/src/components/epic-choice-rows/EpicChoiceRow.en.ts"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-choice-rows/EpicChoiceRow.en.ts" code>EpicChoiceRow.en.ts</></>.
	</>

	<section label="1. Example">
		<icon slot="icon" name="eye"/>
		<text paragraph>Live: the real element, drawn by the epics pack this page loads. Off a details page's own address nothing is saved or sent: Send says so.</>
		<text class="spell-choices-rule" paragraph>What a class holds or works out: <text code>is</> / <text code>has</>.</>
		<html>
			<epic-choice-rows>
				<epic-choice-row name="q1-UIDropdown-187" file="packages/ui/src/components/ui-dropdown/UIDropdown.tsx" line="187" purpose="menu open" note="already `is`:  stays" current="this.isOpen()" recommended="this.isOpen()"></>
				<epic-choice-row name="q1-LoadableComponent-70" file="packages/ui/src/elements/LoadableComponent.tsx" line="70" purpose="save in flight" current="this.saving.get()" recommended="this.isSaving.get()"></>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="2. Markup">
		<icon slot="icon" name="code"/>
		<text paragraph>choice page · a row:</>
		<markdown>
			```html
			<epic-choice-row
			  name="q1-LoadableComponent-70"
			  file="packages/ui/src/elements/LoadableComponent.tsx"
			  line="70"
			  purpose="save in flight"
			  current="this.saving.get()"
			  recommended="this.isSaving.get()"
			></epic-choice-row>
			```
		</>
	</>

	<section label="3. Where it goes">
		<icon slot="icon" name="layer group"/>
		<list bulleted>
			<item>In an <link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-choice-rows-html" link="/epic-choice-rows"><text code>&lt;epic-choice-rows&gt;</></>, which lays it out.</>
			<item>No children: everything is in its attributes.</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="4. Attributes">
		<icon slot="icon" name="table columns"/>
		<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped" unstackable>
			<row header>
				<cell>Name</>
				<cell>Values</>
				<cell>Meaning</>
				<cell>Required</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>name</>
				</>
				<cell>text</>
				<cell>Its id in the rows file (<text code>q1-UISection-169</>): its box's key in the draft and the answer.</>
				<cell>yes</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>file</>
				</>
				<cell>text</>
				<cell>Its file, from the repo's root: the File cell opens it in VS Code.</>
				<cell/>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>line</>
				</>
				<cell>a number</>
				<cell>Its line in <text code>file</>, from 1.</>
				<cell/>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>purpose</>
				</>
				<cell>text</>
				<cell>What it's for, in words a reader new to it follows; `<text code/>code<text code/>` in it shows as code.</>
				<cell/>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>note</>
				</>
				<cell>text</>
				<cell>A short why, small, in the Explanation column, last; its line breaks show, and `<text code/>code<text code/>` in it shows as code.</>
				<cell/>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>current</>
				</>
				<cell>text</>
				<cell>How the use site reads today (<text code>this.isOpen()</>).</>
				<cell/>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>recommended</>
				</>
				<cell>text</>
				<cell>Claude's call, the box's starting text; the same as <text code>current</> for a row that stays.</>
				<cell/>
			</>
		</>

		<section label="Parts" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing open="false">
			<text paragraph>A part is a piece of what the element draws in its shadow root (its own hidden markup), named so a stylesheet can reach it: <text code>epic-choice-row::part(base)</>.</>
			<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped" unstackable>
				<row header>
					<cell>Part</>
					<cell>What it is</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>base</>
					</>
					<cell>Its cells, laid out on its table's columns.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>order</>
					</>
					<cell>The Order cell, in a table you put in order: its place, and its move up / move down buttons.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>up</>
					</>
					<cell>The move up button: it swaps places with the row above.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>down</>
					</>
					<cell>The move down button: it swaps places with the row below.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>file</>
					</>
					<cell>The File cell: the file's name and line, a link into VS Code; its folder under it.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>purpose</>
					</>
					<cell>The Purpose cell: the purpose, and <text code>stays</> when it stays.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>note</>
					</>
					<cell>The Explanation cell, last: the note; empty for a row without one, in a table where others have one.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>current</>
					</>
					<cell>The Current cell: today's text, as code.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>pick</>
					</>
					<cell>The Recommended cell: the box, and the reset button once it differs.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>box</>
					</>
					<cell>The <text code>&lt;ui-textarea grow&gt;</>: one line of text, wrapping and growing; Enter adds no line.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>reset</>
					</>
					<cell>The round button putting the recommendation back.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>comment</>
					</>
					<cell>The comment box under the box, a <text code>&lt;ui-textarea grow&gt;</>: your choice or notes on this row, free text; Enter adds a line. Saved and sent with the box.</>
				</>
			</>
		</>

		<section label="States" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing open="false">
			<text paragraph>A state is a word the element sets on itself while something is true, for styling: <text code>epic-choice-row:state(changed)</>. Never written in the file.</>
			<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped" unstackable>
				<row header>
					<cell>State</>
					<cell>When</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>changed</>
					</>
					<cell>Its box differs from the recommendation: orange.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>stays</>
					</>
					<cell>Claude recommends no change.</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="5. How it looks">
		<icon slot="icon" name="palette"/>
		<list bulleted>
			<item>Order, in a table with <text code>reorder</> (epic <text code>epic-workflow</> P15): its place, then two small grey chevrons, move up and move down, dimmed at either end. A move swaps it with its neighbour, and the focus stays on the button pressed.</>
			<item>File: the file's name and line, a link that opens VS Code at the line; its folder under it, small.</>
			<item>Purpose: a few words or a sentence, <text code>stays</> when Claude would keep it.</>
			<item>The box: monospace, one line of text that wraps and grows. Changed: orange, an orange edge on the row, and a round button putting the recommendation back.</>
			<item>The comment box, under it: the cell's whole width, in the text's own font, empty, a quiet placeholder ("Your choice, notes ..."). It grows with its text; Enter adds a line. A comment is no change to the box: the row stays as it was, and the comment goes with the draft and "Do it" on its own.</>
			<item>Explanation, the last column: the note in small grey print, its line breaks kept. Only when some row of the table has a note.</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="6. Written by">
		<icon slot="icon" name="terminal"/>
		<list bulleted>
			<item><text code>epic choices create</>: one per row of the rows file, by file then line (in the file's order without the File column).</>
			<item>Older pages: the migration step <text code>answer-elements</>.</>
		</>
	</>
	<html>
		<footer class="site-page-footer">
			<ui-divider></>
